                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_448">Pipewell,
                        Northamptonshire, Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>An
                        inscription in a 14th century hand, verso of last leaf, records the
                        presentation of this manuscript to the Abbot of Pipewell, <persName
                           role="fmo">Thomas Burton</persName>: <q>Istut Psalterium per manus
                              <persName role="scr">Iohannis Tryguran</persName> Archid' detur
                           reuerendo patri et domino domino abbati de pippewell Thome Burton</q>
                        (from Barnard's catalogue).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">Lt-Col. W. E.
                        Moss</persName>, Sonning, who bought from <persName role="fmo">P.
                        Barnard</persName> of Tunbridge Wells. See his catalogue 92 (Aug 1914), no.
                     331.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sold (Sotheby, lot 1171) 8 March 1937 to
                     Marks &amp; Co. (£5).This was the last known provenance according to the second
                     edition of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Identical with Schoenberg Database of
                     Manuscripts <ref target="https://sdbm.library.upenn.edu/manuscripts/187"
                        >SDBM_MS_187</ref>, last seen at Sotheby's in 1995.</provenance>
